  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want the **« + » message-actions button** in each message header to be as big and as easy to hit as in legacy. Today it is a small text glyph that is hard to tap. (Operator feedback, 2026-11-17, device screenshot: the « + » at the right of the header is visibly small.)\n\n### Today (dev-swift)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicHTMLBuilder.swift:163-164`: `<button class=\"menu-button\" …>+</button>`, a **text** « + ».\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Resources/reader.css:184`: `font-size: min(1.4em, 32px); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1; min-width: 2.2em; padding: 0.5em 0.4em; margin: -0.5em 0`. The glyph is a font « + », whose arms are short and thin at that size.\n- #594 (operator, 2026-11-15) brought back « the legacy glyph » in the accent colour, citing `templatev2.htm:6`. It kept a text character, while legacy draws an image.\n\n### Legacy @ 87fe0d1c (measured)\n\n- `templatev2.htm`: `<div class=\"right\" onClick=\"touchHeaderMessage(this,'message')\"> + </div>`. The text is hidden behind a background image in the iOS 7+ sheets.\n- `SuperHFRplus/Assets/HTML/style-liste-dark.css:590-595` (also `style-liste-oled.css:591`; the retina sheets at `:76` use the `@2x` image): `.ios7 .message .header .right { height: 32px; width: 32px; float: right; background: transparent url(plus-tinted.png) no-repeat 0 3px; }`.\n- `SuperHFRplus/Assets/UI/plus-tinted@2x.png`, measured: 64×64 px, so **32×32 pt**. The drawn « + » is **16×16 pt** (opaque bbox 16…48 px at @2x), with a **2 pt** stroke (4 px at @2x), centred, in the accent colour. The tap area is the 32×32 pt box, inside a header row that is itself tappable (`touchHeaderMessage`).\n\n### Scope\n\n1. Draw the button's « + » at legacy's size: a **16×16 pt** cross with **2 pt** strokes, centred in a **tap box of at least 32×32 pt** (44×44 pt if the header height allows it without growing the row; say which in the PR). Use inline SVG or CSS lines in `var(--action)`, not a font glyph, so the size does not depend on the font or on Dynamic Type. Whether it scales with the reader text size: legacy does not; say what you chose.\n2. Keep the accessibility label « Actions du message de … » and `aria-haspopup`. Keep the vertical alignment with the pseudo and the date (no header height change), and keep the #594 accent colour.\n3. Check every theme (light, dark, oled), compact density and the Duo cover screen.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- An app-hosted WebKit test: the button's box is at least 32×32 CSS px, the drawn cross is 16 px with 2 px strokes, and the header height is unchanged from before (±1 px).\n- A `### Ledger` `changelog` entry: a parity fix citing `style-liste-dark.css:590-595` and the measured asset.\n- Tests fail without the change.\n\n### Device check (for the #893 general review)\n\nThe « + » looks like legacy's and is easy to hit with a thumb.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
